From 6537dd5791de388faf7b3a06e320e7a0733bd992 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Lee <ethantlee21@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:14:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] embedded: add a manual surface that the host feeds with
 bytes, with no pty

A surface made with manual_io has no pty and no child process. The host
feeds the terminal with ghostty_surface_feed. Input and terminal replies
go out through manual_write. Each size change goes out through
manual_resize. Selection, search, scrollback, links, OSC handling and
every GHOSTTY_ACTION callback work as for a pty surface, because they
read the terminal and not the pty.

Add the manual termio backend (termio/Manual.zig), the three fields of
ghostty_surface_config_s, and ghostty_surface_feed. A normal surface
is unchanged.
